## 1. The two priors (each attacks a specific characterized failure)

| Prior | Attacks | Mechanism | Precedent | Feasibility |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| **Spatial (ET-occurrence atlas)** | Hallucination / false positives | Down-weight enhancement in low-ET-probability locations (ventricles, brainstem, cavity margins). A bright vessel in an implausible place gets suppressed. | ET-occurrence map built in SRI24 space from 1,251 BraTS21 cases (Frontiers/PMC 2023); Prastawa atlas + subject tumor prior. | HIGH — BraTS is pre-registered to SRI24, so no per-case registration. Build the map by averaging training-fold ET masks. |
| **Topological (cubical PH)** | Discrimination (tumor vs non-tumor enhancement) | A solid tumor blob and a thin vessel/margin can share intensity but differ in topology. PH detects the characteristic persistent, roughly-spherical ET component and suppresses low-persistence thin structures. | Train-free cubical-PH glioblastoma segmentation exploiting ET's "characteristic spherical shape" (JMIV, May 2026). | MODERATE — existing cubical-PH tooling from the thesis TDA work; needs a PH library (GUDHI) on the score/enhancement map. |

(A third option — a statistical shape model via PCA on SDFs — is deferred; the two above
map most directly onto the two failures the baseline exposed.)

### Integration modes (test more than one — they're different experiments)

Each prior can enter the pipeline at three points. Ablate them:

1. **Pre-filter ("layer before"):** the prior restricts WHERE / WHICH-SHAPE the intensity
   methods may look, before they run (spatial: mask to plausible-location; topological:
   seed only from persistent blob-like components). This is the user's "persistence layer
   before." Clean, modular, easy to ablate.
2. **Post-filter:** run the existing methods, then suppress predicted components that are
   in low-probability locations (spatial) or topologically implausible (topological).
   Directly targets the FP-component explosion.
3. **MAP / Bayesian combination:** posterior ∝ prior(location or topology) × intensity
   likelihood; threshold the posterior. The principled version.

