## 3. Checkpoints (staged, gated — same discipline as the whole project)

Each stage: STOP, report against acceptance criteria, wait for review. Build priors on
training folds only; evaluate on held-out fold. Never build a prior on a case you score.

### Stage P0 — Infrastructure & baseline lock (no priors yet)
- Confirm the corrected Stage-4 metric is a reusable, callable function (lesion-wise FP-
  aware Dice + FP burden), so every Phase-2 config is scored identically to the baseline.
- Freeze the baseline comparison numbers per stratum + FP axis (the targets to beat).
- Confirm the 5 cohort folds are usable: report ET-present count per fold (priors need
  real tumors to train on).
ACCEPTANCE: metric function reproduces the Stage-4 baseline table exactly; fold ET-present
counts reported.

### Stage P1 — Spatial prior (ET-occurrence atlas). MOST FEASIBLE; targets FP.
- Build the atlas: for each held-out fold, average the ET masks of the OTHER folds' ET-
  present cases (in SRI24/BraTS space — verify all cohort cases share the grid confirmed
  in the geometry check) into a voxel-wise ET-occurrence probability map. Smooth lightly.
- VERIFY the atlas is sane: it should be near-zero in ventricles/brainstem, higher in
  white-matter middle/posterior. Render it. Report the ET-occurrence value at the two
  irreducible cases' (00533/02078) mislocalized seed locations — expect LOW (that's the
  point: those non-tumor structures sit where ET is improbable).
- Apply in all 3 integration modes; score on the corrected metric.
- KEY QUESTION: does the spatial prior reduce absent-case flood rate / FP burden WITHOUT
  harming detection on present cases? Report the FP-axis delta and the lesion-wise delta.
ACCEPTANCE: atlas verified sane; comparison table (baseline vs 3 spatial modes) on the
corrected metric, per stratum + FP axis. STOP.

### Stage P2 — Topological prior (cubical PH). Targets discrimination.
- On the enhancement/score map, compute cubical persistence (GUDHI or existing thesis
  tooling). Identify persistent, blob-like components (high-persistence H0/H2 features)
  vs low-persistence thin structures.
- Apply in pre-filter mode (seed intensity methods only from persistent blob components)
  and post-filter mode (drop topologically-implausible predicted components).
- VERIFY on a known case: on a case where a thin vessel/margin is being segmented as ET,
  confirm the PH filter assigns it low persistence and suppresses it, while preserving the
  persistent tumor blob. Show the persistence diagram + the before/after mask.
- KEY QUESTION: does the topological prior improve dominant-lesion-found rate / lesion-wise
  detection by discriminating blob-tumor from thin-non-tumor enhancement?
ACCEPTANCE: PH filter verified on a known confound case; comparison table (baseline vs topo
modes) on the corrected metric. STOP.

### Stage P3 — Combined + final comparative
- Test spatial + topological together (best mode of each).
- Assemble the FULL comparison table: baseline best, each prior × mode, combined —
  lesion-wise by stratum, dominant-found rate, FP burden, FP flood rate.
- Statistical rigor: bootstrap CIs over cohort cases; paired tests vs baseline. State
  which improvements are real vs within noise.
- Write the honest headline per H1/H2/H3, reporting whichever outcome occurred.
ACCEPTANCE: full comparative table with CIs; per-hypothesis conclusion. STOP.

